{
  "why": "Every way the editor's Tiptap mark rules accept a mark — canonical tags, synonyms (<b>, <i>, <del>, <strike>) and CSS styles — with the marks the text X must carry. src/ui/proseMarkSynonyms.test.ts runs each case through the real editor schema and also requires every editor parse rule to be exercised; relay/src/sync/prose_fixture_tests.rs requires the relay parser to produce the same marks. A synonym on one side only is the drift this file catches (JP-514). A case may also declare `blocks`, the number of top-level blocks both sides must produce.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "strong",
      "html": "<p><strong>X</strong></p>",
      "marks": [
        "bold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "b",
      "html": "<p><b>X</b></p>",
      "marks": [
        "bold"
      ],
      "why": "A synonym the relay used to unwrap: the agent's bold vanished with ok:true (JP-514)."
    },
    {
      "name": "b_with_font_weight_normal_is_not_bold",
      "html": "<p><b style=\"font-weight: normal\">X</b></p>",
      "marks": [],
      "why": "Google Docs wraps every paste in <b style=\"font-weight:normal\">; treating it as bold would make whole pastes bold."
    },
    {
      "name": "b_with_font_weight_400_is_still_bold",
      "html": "<p><b style=\"font-weight: 400\">X</b></p>",
      "marks": [
        "bold"
      ],
      "why": "ProseMirror applies an element's style to the inherited marks before the tag's own mark, so 400 clears nothing here."
    },
    {
      "name": "span_font_weight_bold",
      "html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: bold\">X</span></p>",
      "marks": [
        "bold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "span_font_weight_600",
      "html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600\">X</span></p>",
      "marks": [
        "bold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "span_font_weight_300_is_not_bold",
      "html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 300\">X</span></p>",
      "marks": []
    },
    {
      "name": "font_weight_400_clears_an_outer_bold",
      "html": "<p><strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400\">X</span></strong></p>",
      "marks": []
    },
    {
      "name": "em",
      "html": "<p><em>X</em></p>",
      "marks": [
        "italic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "i",
      "html": "<p><i>X</i></p>",
      "marks": [
        "italic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "i_with_font_style_normal_is_not_italic",
